  era: "c. 2800 BCE onwards \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Harappan agriculture
  text: Farmers grew wheat, barley, pulses, sesame and cotton; the Harappans were among the earliest to grow cotton. A ploughed field was found at Kalibangan, and a terracotta plough model at Banawali. Rice and millets appear at some sites.
